b=Book('06','Rebuild Plan & Data Reference','Rebuild-Data-Reference','A dependency-ordered implementation manual, acceptance gates, complete typed schema and migration index.');b.intro()
b.section('How to rebuild from scratch','''Rebuild Mellox around its invariants before copying its screens. Identity must be explicit, workspace data must stay isolated, paid work must be metered exactly once, generated work must remain reviewable, and long-lived side effects must survive process restarts. The order below is a recommended dependency plan inferred from current implementation, not a committed delivery schedule or team estimate.

Keep the six volumes and the source snapshot together. Volume 01 defines behavior, volume 02 maps architecture/contracts, volume 03 defines AI execution, volume 04 defines billing, volume 05 defines operations, and this volume provides implementation order plus the exact checked-in table/column and migration indexes.

PDFs cannot encode private vendor accounts, production environment values, invoices or future product decisions that were not supplied. A clean rebuild also needs a source repository and the owning provider accounts. Recreate the public contracts and invariants; do not assume an older audit, deprecated adapter or proposed feature is required merely because a historical file remains.''',('docs/documentation-maintenance.md','src/server/route.ts','src/lib/billing/catalog.ts','supabase/migrations'))
b.section('Phase 1 - repository and deployable skeleton','''Deliver the Next.js/React/TypeScript skeleton, current styling primitives, app/public route split, server-only boundary, Supabase clients, environment validation and a Railway-compatible container. Use the checked-in lockfile versions as the reproducibility baseline. Read the installed Next.js documentation before changing framework configuration or routing.

Create development, isolated test and production environments with separate data and credentials. Establish a migration mechanism, release manifest and health identity before paid features. Install native tools for the selected runtime: Chromium, FFmpeg and the image-metadata dependencies when those capabilities are enabled. Optional Redis is valuable for shared cache/rate behavior across replicas, but durable truth stays in PostgreSQL.

Acceptance: fresh build starts with the intended port; missing required production variables fail clearly; /health is live; safe health/readiness paths report the release identity and unavailable capabilities honestly; a browser bundle contains no server credentials.''',('package.json','package-lock.json','Dockerfile','src/server/env.ts','src/instrumentation.ts','next.config.ts'))
b.section('Phase 2 - auth, workspaces, roles and account ownership','''Implement signup/login, confirmation, password recovery, logout and workspace creation/listing. Wire canonical workspace routes, provider context and query-key isolation. Implement membership, invitation and role transitions with owner protection and operation-specific checks. Introduce the owner's billing account relationship before users create multiple brands.

Persist profiles, workspaces, members, invites, sources and connections through the canonical schema. Enable RLS, prohibit unsafe workspace reassignment, and reserve service-role queries for explicit server paths. A supplied workspace or item ID must be authorized every time; a remembered browser selection is only UI state.

Acceptance: outsider reads/writes fail even with real UUIDs; an editor cannot act as owner; a viewer cannot spend; a delayed response cannot replace another workspace's content; password-recovery replay and sign-out failure do not present false success; owner/account mapping remains stable across workspace changes.''',('src/server/workspaces','src/server/fns/workspaces.ts','src/lib/workspace','src/integrations/supabase','supabase/migrations'))
b.section('Phase 3 - billing, AI gateway and durable accounting','''Build the pure commercial catalog and entitlement resolver, then account allowances, restricted grants, holds, capture/release, replay keys, expiry and monthly windows. Keep general credits, video units and message counters separate. Add availability gates for later features. Integrate Stripe through server-created prices/checkouts and verified replay-safe events; do not let the browser set money amounts.

Add the AI task registry, provider gateway, spend controls, usage events, normalized errors, cache and rate limiting. Route call sites by task label, not arbitrary model names. Add provider-reported cost handling and safe estimate fallback. Model overrides must remain deliberate and auditable.

Acceptance: identical idempotency keys cannot charge twice; streaming cancellation releases only safely releasable funds; ambiguous capture is replayed safely; provider outages are visible; missing billing schema does not make production unlimited; fallback records the model actually used; an unknown test task fails registry coverage.''',('src/lib/billing/catalog.ts','src/server/billing','src/server/ai','src/lib/ai-gateway.server.ts','src/server/platform'))
b.section('Phase 4 - Brain, memory and assistant','''Build Brand DNA extraction/editing and current Brand Look, then competitor/market source stores, audience groups and strategy confirmation. Implement memory rules, provenance, removal markers, temporary expiry and the workspace use-memory switch. Retrieval of stored knowledge is the persistent-context mechanism; no custom foundation-model training is required by this architecture.

Add chat streaming, research and read tools. Store offered write actions server-side with explicit role recheck and single-run transition. Persist reply metadata for reload. Memory changes use the dedicated decision rules; retrieved untrusted data cannot authorize arbitrary writes.

Acceptance: an unconfirmed strategy never reaches a generator; a hallucinated competitor/source is rejected; changed memory invalidates context caches; removed memories stay removed; a read tool cannot mutate; duplicate action-button clicks run once; messages and tool data remain workspace-scoped.''',('src/server/brain','src/server/strategy','src/server/memory','src/server/chat','src/lib/memory','src/lib/strategy'))
b.section('Phase 5 - Studio, assets and editorial workflow','''Build content_items and asset persistence before individual generators. Implement durable studio_jobs with leases and recovery, then social text, scripts, ads, articles, carousels, Stories and image generation. Reuse shared context and brand rules, deterministic renderers, review stages and metadata.

Add the library, calendar, versioned edits, approval statuses, conflict detection and cancel-before-edit behavior for in-flight delivery. Persist media in private R2 through canonical workspace keys, while supporting existing legacy storage identities. Canva round trips produce new versioned assets, never overwrite originals. Notion is optional manual planning exchange with preview and conflict handling.

Acceptance: successful text/image work becomes a saved draft; a partial job settles its own billing; restart recovery does not lose accepted provider tasks; asset URLs cannot cross tenants; changing kind invalidates approval; stale saves return 409; pending local edits block approval until saved; scheduled work cannot be rewritten behind the provider's back.''',('src/server/studio','src/server/assets','src/server/fns/content.ts','src/server/connectors/canva','src/server/connectors/notion','supabase/migrations/20261018090000_content_kind_approval.sql'))
b.section('Phase 6 - social, website publishing and measurement','''Choose Post for Me or deliberately provision the separate SDR path. Implement account connection, current network metadata, media validation, schedule/publish/cancel, signature-verified callbacks, frame-level Story results, idempotent delivery and polling/reconciliation. Do not build the retired SocialAPI provider as a new default.

Implement website connection, source ownership and article publishing as distinct flows. GitHub changes produce reviewed PRs; CMS actions respect actual connector capabilities. Then connect GA4/GSC and social feed metrics with durable sync runs, attribution metadata and failure states.

Acceptance: unapproved content is refused; a duplicate webhook cannot regress a terminal publication; partial Story retry sends only unresolved frames with unchanged source identity; missing network metrics stay unavailable; website-source failure marks an incomplete queue; a social post does not deduct general AI credits.''',('src/lib/postforme','src/lib/feature-flags.ts','src/server/social','src/server/articles','src/server/analytics','src/server/fns/publish.ts'))
b.section('Phase 7 - video and composition','''Add product extraction, concepts, notes and plan-aware model routing. Share the capability registry with validation and UI; native duration, aspect ratio, resolution, audio and references depend on the selected provider. Quote and reserve video allowance using routed cost, not a hard-coded generic price.

Persist accepted provider/model/task identity before polling. Use provider fallback only after definite compatible refusal. Add the composition table, revision leases, segmented prompts, clip safety checks and FFmpeg assembly for longer outputs. Store and settle the final asset once. Keep cancellation behavior consistent with provider acceptance and financial state.

Acceptance: long output survives an application restart; uncertain submit cannot double-spend on another provider; a plan-locked model is not selected; preview and held quote agree; accepted clips are not recreated after polling; unsupported references fail explicitly; partial/unsafe output does not become a publishable asset.''',('src/lib/ugc','src/server/ugc','src/server/billing/ugc-async.server.ts','src/server/ugc/providers/composition.server.ts','supabase/migrations/20261021090000_video_compositions.sql'))
b.section('Phase 8 - visibility, fixes and controlled experiments','''Implement the public-URL-safe crawler, structured evidence, stable deterministic GEO rules, weighted scoring, finding fingerprints, monitors and verification. Add optional rendering and AI probes behind explicit gates. Keep tracked prompt observation history separate from deterministic technical site scores.

Add source ownership, proposal grounding, exact reviewed patches, PR creation and post-change checks before allowing an engineer to modify a site. Build Proof Engine only after source writes and Google page-level data are reliable. Current eligibility includes at least thirty pages, fifty-six complete pre-period days, concentration and power checks, balanced assignment, and final checkpoints from day twenty-one through forty-two. These source constants should not be weakened to obtain an attractive result.

Acceptance: all-pass applicable site reaches the expected score; N/A never deducts; score versions are not compared as ordinary deltas; blocked training crawlers alone do not count as blocked search access; provider failure is not a visibility gap; approval cannot resolve a finding; missing/incomplete experiment data remains inconclusive.''',('src/lib/geo','src/server/geo','src/lib/experiments/constants.ts','src/lib/experiments/evaluate.ts','src/server/experiments'))
b.section('Phase 9 - learning, Autopilot, agencies and assistants','''Add audience outcome calibration and controlled reuse of measured content. Current calibration requires at least one hundred views, eight comparator posts, eight prediction/outcome pairs and bounded shrinkage before corrections. Pure scoring numbers remain separate from model-generated rationale.

Build Autopilot on the same Studio, content, publication and billing services. Plan slots around existing calendar work, ground picks to stored sources, obey weekly spend limits and approval mode, expire missed pieces, then measure and learn. The agency view aggregates allowed workspaces without weakening tenant boundaries.

Expose the existing operations through MCP with OAuth, per-workspace access and change gates, rate limits, cleaned outputs and append-only call history. Add staff controls with explicit permissions, MFA and audited overrides. A commercial SSO/API product remains separate future work until implemented.

Acceptance: automatic-mode policy never broadens itself; new opportunities wait for review; existing posts prevent duplicate slots; article delivery still requires approval; stopping a program blocks future work; assistant tools cannot invoke excluded administration or unapproved publication; staff support access is narrow and audited.''',('src/lib/audience/calibration.ts','src/server/autopilot','src/lib/autopilot','src/server/mcp','src/server/admin'))
b.section('End-to-end acceptance matrix')
b.table(['Scenario','Required observable result','Owning layer'],[['Brand A user requests Brand B row','Denied before privileged provider or data operation','Route/RPC + RLS'],['Same Generate click submitted twice','One durable job and one financial settlement','Job + meter replay keys'],['Process dies after provider accepted render','Stored task can resume; no blind second submit','Provider + composition store'],['Caption save races approval','Revision conflict or serialized correct approval','Content service + database'],['Post type changes after approval','Approval invalidated','Database trigger'],['Publish callback arrives out of order','Newer terminal truth survives','Webhook/reconciler'],['Story frame fails after other frames succeeded','Only unresolved unchanged frames retried','Post for Me adapter'],['Expired media URL opened','Authorized route can issue fresh short-lived URL','Asset storage'],['GEO fix approved but not visible live','Finding remains unresolved/inconclusive','Verification engine'],['Audience content changed','Old prediction no longer shown as matching','Exact fingerprint cache'],['Experiment lacks sufficient complete days','No final positive verdict manufactured','Pure experiment evaluation'],['Plan falls to Free','Preserved content, constrained excess brands/spend','Entitlements and account lifecycle'],['Admin without required permission/MFA','Denied and refusal audited','Admin route kernel'],['MCP workspace changes disabled','Read works only where enabled; write/spend denied','MCP gate + app services']],[1.6,2,1.2]);b.source('tests','src/server','supabase/migrations')
b.section('Concrete request contracts and continuation behavior')
b.h('Start an AI Visibility scan')
b.code('POST /api/geo/scans\nAuthorization: Bearer <member access token>\nContent-Type: application/json\n\n{"workspaceId":"<UUID>","url":"https://example.com",\n "mode":"full","trigger":"manual",\n "probes":false,"idempotencyKey":"<8-100 characters>"}')
b.p('Editor required. URL text is 1-2000 characters and safe-fetch validates the real destination. Mode defaults full; trigger defaults manual and allows manual/chat/rescan. Probes and idempotencyKey are optional. Full non-rescan work checks monthly scan limits. Success is 201 {scan}; an active-scan conflict is 409 with activeScanId. Full work continues in a durable scan and is polled through its ID; quick work gets a bounded inline drive.')
b.h('Studio and UGC contract ownership')
b.p('POST /api/studio/jobs uses CreateJobSchema in src/lib/studio/jobs.ts, editor role and media-dependent rate limits. It returns {job}, with X-Billing-Balance when available. GET on the same route reads recent jobs for a workspace so UI can resume after reload. UGC POST /api/ugc/renders uses StartRenderBody in src/lib/ugc/schemas.ts; choices and a per-click replay key are client inputs, but price, allowance, model capability and activation remain server decisions. These richer schemas should be reused directly instead of approximating them from a static example.')
b.source('src/app/api/geo/scans/route.ts','src/app/api/studio/jobs/route.ts','src/lib/studio/jobs.ts','src/app/api/ugc/renders/route.ts','src/lib/ugc/schemas.ts')
b.section('Current-state corrections and decision backlog')
b.table(['Older / ambiguous claim','Current blueprint treatment'],[['SocialAPI as active social provider','Retired by provider selector; Post for Me configured first, optional SDR.'],['Social publication uses general credits','No general-credit charge; current monthly fair-use controls apply.'],['Brand Styles as parallel style library','Current Brain/Brand Look replaces that earlier design.'],['Video is always an eight-second single task','Current output defaults ten seconds; supports composition up to sixty.'],['Variation falls back to OpenRouter Grok','Current fallback is six-second Veo Lite.'],['Every feature waits for every post approval','Current explicit fully automatic mode can send qualifying plain/image content.'],['Scale SSO/API is implemented because of tagline','Catalog explicitly marks commercial SSO/API later.'],['Python adapter names define the main app models','Separate runtime; main task registry owns main-app defaults.'],['Amplify/Lightsail/tunnel docs prove current host','Owner confirms Railway; exact service details remain unverified.'],['Old forecasts are actual margins','Use current catalog estimates and measured invoices separately.'],['Model default is necessarily production model','Environment/admin overrides and actual returned model may differ.'],['A file or catalog entry proves production ready','Requires applied migration, credentials, flags, permissions and validation.']],[2,3]);b.source('src/lib/feature-flags.ts','src/lib/billing/catalog.ts','src/lib/ugc/models.ts','src/lib/ugc/duration.ts','src/server/ai/task-models.ts')
b.p('Recommended backlog: fill production inventory and restore policy first; verify provider readiness and remaining schema deployment; align stale canonical guides with current code; validate quote/capability boundaries; maintain generated contract/schema references in CI; only then schedule catalog later features. These are recommendations, not owner-approved launch commitments.')
b.section('Data dictionary conventions',new=True)
b.p('The following is the complete 179-table Row-type dictionary extracted from the checked-in Supabase TypeScript schema. It includes field names, TypeScript scalar/union types and declared relationships. string can represent SQL text, UUID or timestamp; number can represent several SQL numeric types. Json is a schema-less TypeScript JSON value, whose business shape must be read from feature contracts and migrations. Nullability appears as | null. SQL defaults, check constraints, indexes, triggers, grants and exact RLS policies are not encoded by this Row dictionary.')
b.p('Treat this as a navigation and reconstruction reference with the migration history, not runnable replacement DDL. It may include compatibility objects still represented in generated types. No table contents, customer rows or secret credential values are included. Service-only credential tables are named so their separation can be rebuilt, but must never become browser-readable just because they appear here.')
b.source('src/integrations/supabase/types.ts','supabase/migrations')
for t in sorted(D['tables'],key=lambda x:x['name']):
    b.h(t['name']);b.p('; '.join(c['name']+': '+re.sub(r'\s+',' ',c['type']) for c in t['columns']),'small')
    rel=t['relations'];matches=list(re.finditer(r'foreignKeyName:\s*"([^"]+)";\s*columns:\s*\[([^\]]*)\];\s*isOneToOne:\s*(\w+);\s*referencedRelation:\s*"([^"]+)";\s*referencedColumns:\s*\[([^\]]*)\]',rel))
    if matches:
        for m in matches:b.p('FK '+m[1]+': ('+m[2].replace('"','')+') -> '+m[4]+' ('+m[5].replace('"','')+'); one-to-one '+m[3],'small')
    elif rel.strip() not in ('[]',''):b.p('Relationships: '+re.sub(r'\s+',' ',rel),'small')
b.section('Latest SQL addition not yet in generated types')
b.p('The source audit found one table created by the current migration sequence that is not represented in the checked-in generated Row dictionary: video_compositions. Keep this SQL-only addition alongside the 179 typed tables. Regenerate types after applying the migration in the intended environment; do not omit the table when rebuilding longer-video support.')
b.table(['Column','Exact SQL declaration'],[['id','uuid PRIMARY KEY'],['revision','integer NOT NULL DEFAULT 0'],['lease_until','timestamptz; nullable'],['state','jsonb NOT NULL'],['created_at','timestamptz NOT NULL DEFAULT now()']],[1,3])
b.p('RLS is enabled. All privileges are revoked from anon and authenticated; service_role receives access. State contains the render request, clip target and render lengths, accepted provider task IDs, provider identity, available video URLs/cost and submission progress. The worker uses revision comparison and lease_until to coordinate writes. Sensitive state must remain server-only.')
